** 8. Fundamental difference between Hough circles and circularity. Which is better and why?**
Hough circle detection

Hough detection searches an image for circular patterns, usually using edge information. It estimates the circle's centre and radius.

OpenCV function: cv2.HoughCircles()

It can detect circles without first extracting a contour for each object.
Circularity

Circularity measures how close an already detected contour is to a perfect circle. It is calculated using the contour's area and perimeter.
\[
C=\frac{4\pi A}{P^2}
\]

Here, \(A\) is the contour area and \(P\) is its perimeter. A perfect circle has circularity 1; irregular shapes generally have lower values.

9. Difference between methods and functions

A function is a reusable block of code that performs a task. A method is a function associated with an object or class.
print() is a function. You call it directly by its name.

Another example is cv2.GaussianBlur(), which is called through the cv2 module.
upper() is a string method. It is called on the string object text.
get() is a dictionary method.

Function	Method
Called independently or through a module	Called on an object or class
May receive an object as an argument	Often operates on the object it belongs to
